WEBVTT

00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:15.030
Any last words?

00:00:15.030 --> 00:00:18.530
There's no need to ask that
question to a mere Taint.

00:00:24.230 --> 00:00:25.690
Dazai- <i>kun</i> ?

00:00:25.690 --> 00:00:27.400
What are you doing?

00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:29.480
I won't let you kill him.

00:00:29.480 --> 00:00:30.900
What?

00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:32.980
Fake or not...

00:00:32.980 --> 00:00:35.690
...he's one of us!

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:35.730
I see.

00:02:35.730 --> 00:02:40.030
I was... Ryunosuke Akutagawa.

00:02:40.030 --> 00:02:41.230
Born...

00:02:46.530 --> 00:02:48.530
Born inside you.

00:02:51.280 --> 00:02:53.730
Episode 12

00:02:54.860 --> 00:02:56.690
Ryunosuke Akutagawa.

00:02:56.690 --> 00:03:01.190
You were a very timid and delicate person.

00:03:01.190 --> 00:03:07.110
You suspected that in their hearts,
everyone hated you.

00:03:07.110 --> 00:03:13.400
So you needed someone who would love you.

00:03:13.400 --> 00:03:15.730
There's something I want to write.

00:03:15.730 --> 00:03:17.780
What is it?

00:03:17.780 --> 00:03:21.980
A novel. A novel that's like a real novel.

00:03:21.980 --> 00:03:24.280
Then write it.

00:03:24.280 --> 00:03:30.150
But I understand that nobody wants it...

00:03:30.150 --> 00:03:37.690
And I know that I can't write
something like Shiga- <i>san</i> .

00:03:37.690 --> 00:03:42.980
You think everything has to be perfect, right?

00:03:42.980 --> 00:03:46.570
Because that's what people want.

00:03:46.570 --> 00:03:48.690
You're too kind.

00:03:48.690 --> 00:03:53.280
You think that you can't
betray people's expectations.

00:03:53.280 --> 00:03:55.610
I'm just afraid they'll be disappointed in me.

00:04:03.070 --> 00:04:07.820
You wanted a friend who
would love everything about you.

00:04:07.820 --> 00:04:12.610
And that's why you created me inside you.

00:04:12.610 --> 00:04:16.610
I was someone you could
always count on to love you.

00:04:16.610 --> 00:04:21.440
And you were my whole world.

00:04:21.440 --> 00:04:28.150
So that's why I wanted to support your strong
but fragile sense of self-respect.

00:04:28.150 --> 00:04:31.480
No matter how many years passed,
or where you went.

00:04:33.190 --> 00:04:37.570
You kept writing. You didn't run from writing.

00:04:40.320 --> 00:04:43.780
No, maybe that's not right.

00:04:43.780 --> 00:04:47.150
It felt to me like you couldn't run.

00:04:47.150 --> 00:04:52.610
It seemed to me like the novels,
like literature, made you its prisoner.

00:04:52.610 --> 00:04:54.610
What do I do?

00:04:54.610 --> 00:04:56.360
What am I?

00:04:56.360 --> 00:04:58.440
What will become of me?

00:04:58.440 --> 00:05:06.900
You knew that writing was wearing you down,
but you could only choose to write.

00:05:06.900 --> 00:05:12.530
Maybe your ultimate fate
was already decided then.

00:05:15.480 --> 00:05:18.480
What do I do?

00:05:18.480 --> 00:05:23.940
I can't go back to being
the Ryunosuke Akutagawa people want.

00:05:23.940 --> 00:05:27.650
Why are you like that?

00:05:27.650 --> 00:05:33.400
Why do you still try to give others
what they want, even now?

00:05:33.400 --> 00:05:38.070
Because it's all I have, I'm sure.

00:05:38.070 --> 00:05:39.980
Because I'm empty.

00:05:39.980 --> 00:05:42.110
The least I can do is have
others think well of me...

00:05:42.110 --> 00:05:43.820
You're not empty!

00:05:43.820 --> 00:05:45.900
You're...

00:05:45.900 --> 00:05:51.610
You're right. You were always on my side.

00:05:51.610 --> 00:05:56.650
Because that's how I made you.

00:05:56.650 --> 00:06:01.440
I'm sorry for forcing you
to live such a useless life.

00:06:01.440 --> 00:06:06.070
Are you trying to make it
so I think well of you, too?

00:06:06.070 --> 00:06:07.690
It's a bad habit.

00:06:10.940 --> 00:06:15.280
You've always been there for me.

00:06:15.280 --> 00:06:18.690
So now, at the end, please grant my wish.

00:06:18.690 --> 00:06:20.280
What?

00:06:20.280 --> 00:06:24.900
Will you strangle me
to death softly, as I sleep?

00:06:50.400 --> 00:06:52.940
And in the end, you...

00:07:02.520 --> 00:07:06.530
"A Dialogue in the Darkness"

00:07:03.280 --> 00:07:06.070
The draft you left behind was a dialogue

00:07:06.070 --> 00:07:10.400
between you and another you,
who denied everything you did.

00:07:06.530 --> 00:07:10.530
A Dialogue in the Darkness

00:07:11.570 --> 00:07:18.110
You created me, but you couldn't
even allow me my kindness.

00:07:18.110 --> 00:07:22.400
My only friend, the master who created me...

00:07:22.400 --> 00:07:24.980
You were everything to me.

00:07:24.980 --> 00:07:32.190
I hate the novels that took you
prisoner and wouldn't let you go!

00:07:28.550 --> 00:07:32.550
A Dialogue in the Darkness

00:07:32.190 --> 00:07:36.070
I despise the curse called literature
that limited the way you could live.

00:07:38.190 --> 00:07:42.730
I was only a creature of
Ryunosuke Akutagawa's imagination.

00:07:42.730 --> 00:07:46.400
I was supposed to disappear at your death.

00:07:46.400 --> 00:07:49.820
But then they appeared.

00:07:57.650 --> 00:07:59.190
Where am I?

00:08:00.360 --> 00:08:02.280
Was it you who called?

00:08:03.940 --> 00:08:05.320
What?

00:08:05.320 --> 00:08:08.230
You called us here.

00:08:08.230 --> 00:08:10.360
What are you saying?

00:08:10.360 --> 00:08:12.570
Who are you?

00:08:12.570 --> 00:08:16.440
The Taints. That is what we are called.

00:08:16.440 --> 00:08:17.980
Taints.

00:08:17.980 --> 00:08:21.610
We taint all literature.

00:08:21.610 --> 00:08:25.570
We destroy all literature.

00:08:25.570 --> 00:08:29.900
That is why we exist.

00:08:29.900 --> 00:08:32.820
Destroy literature?

00:08:32.820 --> 00:08:35.230
Why would you do that?

00:08:35.230 --> 00:08:38.860
Literature awakens the feelings of men.

00:08:38.860 --> 00:08:43.320
But when an individual's
sentiments are awakened,

00:08:43.320 --> 00:08:47.570
eventually they'll become diverse
and come to reject others.

00:08:47.570 --> 00:08:51.980
Literature makes men fools, you could say.

00:08:51.980 --> 00:08:56.400
And the will that created us feared that.

00:08:56.400 --> 00:09:04.610
We Taints are formed of hatred,
jealousy, anger towards literature!

00:09:04.610 --> 00:09:07.360
The feelings of men!

00:09:07.360 --> 00:09:09.940
So you're clusters of emotions?

00:09:09.940 --> 00:09:14.900
Your strong hatred towards
literature brought us here.

00:09:14.900 --> 00:09:19.400
Emotions such as yours make us stronger.

00:09:19.400 --> 00:09:21.440
So you want to absorb me?

00:09:21.440 --> 00:09:24.820
And in exchange, we'll grant your wish.

00:09:24.820 --> 00:09:25.780
Wish?

00:09:25.780 --> 00:09:29.360
You cursed literature.

00:09:29.360 --> 00:09:33.530
So there's a story you want
to destroy, isn't there?

00:09:33.530 --> 00:09:36.690
Destroy it, then!

00:09:35.690 --> 00:09:36.690
A Dialogue in the Darkness

00:09:36.820 --> 00:09:44.190
Destroy it from this world's past and future!

00:09:44.190 --> 00:09:46.360
Past and future?

00:09:46.360 --> 00:09:49.400
Is that really possible?

00:09:49.400 --> 00:09:52.400
The Taints destroy literature.

00:09:52.400 --> 00:09:56.440
Hatred towards literature destroys it.

00:09:56.440 --> 00:09:59.480
An unbelievable story.

00:09:59.480 --> 00:10:02.400
But with my master gone,

00:10:02.400 --> 00:10:05.610
as a creature of imagination,
I'm fated to disappear.

00:10:05.610 --> 00:10:10.610
So now, I'll cling to that one feeble hope.

00:10:10.610 --> 00:10:13.320
Choose. Answer.

00:10:13.320 --> 00:10:18.860
Which story do you wish to curse and destroy?

00:10:18.860 --> 00:10:20.070
I...

00:10:21.690 --> 00:10:26.530
I want to destroy all the stories
of Ryunosuke Akutagawa!

00:10:26.530 --> 00:10:31.820
So you would choose
the works of your own master?

00:10:31.820 --> 00:10:36.190
Do you hate the poor author who created
you as a form of escapism so much?

00:10:36.190 --> 00:10:39.320
Hate? It's the opposite.

00:10:39.320 --> 00:10:43.070
Ryunosuke Akutagawa is my most beloved friend.

00:10:43.070 --> 00:10:45.690
That remains true even now.

00:10:45.690 --> 00:10:47.650
So why?

00:10:47.650 --> 00:10:49.570
Because of that!

00:10:49.570 --> 00:10:55.110
His misery started when he encountered
literature and wrote a book.

00:10:55.110 --> 00:11:00.980
Each time he wrote, he suffered.
Each time he wrote, he gave up a part of himself.

00:11:00.980 --> 00:11:05.940
If he hadn't written any books,
his life would've been happier.

00:11:08.190 --> 00:11:13.070
If he hadn't written any books,
he wouldn't have chosen to die!

00:11:13.070 --> 00:11:17.900
So I will destroy the very fact
that he ever wrote!

00:11:17.900 --> 00:11:22.860
To save the man named Ryunosuke Akutagawa!

00:11:22.860 --> 00:11:29.650
So you would change the author, the cause,
by destroying his books, the result?

00:11:29.650 --> 00:11:35.150
You said that you could remove
them from both past and future.

00:11:35.150 --> 00:11:40.570
Which means that they will have never existed.

00:11:40.570 --> 00:11:43.820
The author will never have written them.

00:11:43.820 --> 00:11:44.900
Am I wrong?

00:11:44.900 --> 00:11:49.190
So you would change the fate of
an author by destroying his books?

00:11:49.190 --> 00:11:50.610
Indeed!

00:11:50.610 --> 00:11:54.150
I want to save the man
named Ryunosuke Akutagawa!

00:11:54.150 --> 00:11:59.110
I will taint literature for his happiness!

00:11:59.110 --> 00:12:00.780
Interesting.

00:12:00.780 --> 00:12:06.940
You're the first person to try to use
the power of the Taints in such a way.

00:12:06.940 --> 00:12:12.230
It would be a shame to absorb you.

00:12:12.230 --> 00:12:13.070
What?

00:12:13.070 --> 00:12:15.070
I've changed my mind.

00:12:15.070 --> 00:12:19.070
We will give you a part of our power.

00:12:19.070 --> 00:12:24.780
You have the soul of an author,
so you may be able to reach that place.

00:12:31.530 --> 00:12:37.110
And in that moment, I absorbed the power
and all of the knowledge of the Taints.

00:12:45.780 --> 00:12:48.690
The Alchemist. The Library.

00:12:48.690 --> 00:12:51.980
The reincarnated authors who gather there.

00:12:51.980 --> 00:12:54.650
I understood it all.

00:12:55.900 --> 00:12:59.570
And so I knew what I must do.

00:12:59.570 --> 00:13:04.730
If you taint a book from the outside,
an author can delve within and stop you.

00:13:06.190 --> 00:13:12.150
So it would be better to go to where those
authors dwelled and eliminate them.

00:13:20.360 --> 00:13:23.820
With this body, born from an author,

00:13:23.820 --> 00:13:28.730
perhaps I could enter the Library
pretending to be one of them.

00:13:32.280 --> 00:13:38.190
The power of the Alchemist to revive
authors was beyond our imagining.

00:13:38.190 --> 00:13:46.820
We managed to get you inside,
but you lost your memories in the process.

00:13:46.820 --> 00:13:50.900
And so I forgot that I was a Taint,

00:13:50.900 --> 00:13:58.030
and fought the Taints as
Ryunosuke Akutagawa, is that it?

00:13:59.860 --> 00:14:01.280
Ironic.

00:14:05.570 --> 00:14:09.280
It seems you've regained it all.

00:14:09.280 --> 00:14:11.860
Yes. I'm fine now.

00:14:25.030 --> 00:14:26.070
What?

00:14:26.070 --> 00:14:29.190
You've finally revealed yourself, huh?

00:14:33.780 --> 00:14:35.150
Akutagawa- <i>sensei</i> !

00:14:45.900 --> 00:14:52.070
After Ryunosuke Akutagawa's death,
you read his epitaph, right?

00:14:53.400 --> 00:14:54.980
On his behalf...

00:14:57.230 --> 00:14:58.860
...I thank you.

00:15:01.030 --> 00:15:05.820
Thank you, best friend of my friend.

00:15:05.820 --> 00:15:07.070
Kikuchi- <i>san</i> !

00:15:26.150 --> 00:15:27.440
No way!

00:15:27.440 --> 00:15:28.650
Hori- <i>kun</i> !

00:15:34.780 --> 00:15:38.320
Uh-oh. This is bad.

00:15:38.320 --> 00:15:39.530
Seriously?

00:15:39.530 --> 00:15:40.690
It's coming!

00:15:40.690 --> 00:15:44.110
This can't be... Akutagawa- <i>sensei</i> !

00:15:44.110 --> 00:15:45.690
Get ready, Dazai!

00:15:45.690 --> 00:15:47.690
That isn't...

00:15:47.690 --> 00:15:49.780
I don't have anything against you.

00:15:49.780 --> 00:15:54.820
But if I let you live,
you'll come to stop me, right?

00:15:54.820 --> 00:15:57.530
So... sorry.

00:16:08.650 --> 00:16:09.820
Oda Saku!

00:16:10.480 --> 00:16:11.690
You bastard!

00:16:20.150 --> 00:16:21.150
Ango!

00:16:28.230 --> 00:16:29.940
Not bad.

00:16:43.360 --> 00:16:44.480
Stop it...

00:16:46.860 --> 00:16:48.980
Stop it, please!

00:16:48.980 --> 00:16:50.900
You won't fight me?

00:16:50.900 --> 00:16:54.280
Why? Why?

00:16:54.280 --> 00:16:56.150
It's simple.

00:16:56.150 --> 00:16:58.360
Because I'm a Taint!

00:16:58.360 --> 00:17:01.730
But even so, you were one of us!

00:17:01.730 --> 00:17:03.070
You were mistaken.

00:17:03.070 --> 00:17:05.030
You were one of us, I know it!

00:17:15.230 --> 00:17:16.650
I don't like those eyes.

00:17:35.570 --> 00:17:36.780
Don't look at me!

00:17:39.980 --> 00:17:44.730
Don't look at me with those eyes!

00:17:50.820 --> 00:17:52.440
They make me upset.

00:18:12.030 --> 00:18:13.980
Why?

00:18:13.980 --> 00:18:15.690
Why would you...

00:18:15.690 --> 00:18:20.610
I don't know myself...

00:18:20.610 --> 00:18:23.610
But you could say...

00:18:23.610 --> 00:18:26.480
...because I felt it.

00:18:26.480 --> 00:18:28.440
Felt it?

00:18:28.440 --> 00:18:32.650
That you love Ryu's books too.

00:18:34.650 --> 00:18:41.940
Dazai... protect literature.
Protect what Ryu created.

00:19:01.320 --> 00:19:03.070
Impossible!

00:19:03.070 --> 00:19:05.900
Akutagawa! You're Akutagawa, right?

00:19:05.900 --> 00:19:07.900
No.

00:19:07.900 --> 00:19:09.650
Now he's just a...

00:19:10.400 --> 00:19:12.570
This looks bad.

00:19:12.570 --> 00:19:15.280
There was still one left.

00:19:18.690 --> 00:19:23.150
So, are you all here?

00:19:23.150 --> 00:19:25.980
That will make it faster.

00:19:25.980 --> 00:19:27.360
Let's run, Sai.

00:19:27.360 --> 00:19:29.900
We can't win without weapons.

00:19:29.900 --> 00:19:31.690
That's the right answer.

00:19:32.650 --> 00:19:34.320
I won't let you escape.

00:19:44.860 --> 00:19:46.110
Oh, no!

00:19:48.940 --> 00:19:50.480
Dive!

00:19:50.480 --> 00:19:51.820
Acting Director?

00:19:51.820 --> 00:19:55.320
Hurry! Get in the book!

00:19:55.320 --> 00:19:57.780
That's right. Inside it...

00:20:01.380 --> 00:20:03.840
"Gears"

00:20:07.980 --> 00:20:10.780
Okay, we can use weapons here.

00:20:25.440 --> 00:20:29.570
Looks like I won't be getting that interview...

00:20:36.030 --> 00:20:38.150
Come and get me!

00:20:38.150 --> 00:20:40.900
Sai, you're being loud!

00:20:40.900 --> 00:20:42.690
Don't worry, Saku.

00:20:42.690 --> 00:20:43.940
I'm here for you.

00:20:43.940 --> 00:20:44.940
Okay.

00:20:47.280 --> 00:20:48.280
Sai!

00:21:08.650 --> 00:21:11.400
You're bad with that gun.

00:21:11.400 --> 00:21:14.690
It's just who I am, damn it!

00:21:18.440 --> 00:21:20.150
Just a little more...

00:21:24.030 --> 00:21:28.110
Just a little more, and your fate will change.

00:21:28.110 --> 00:21:29.860
I can save you...

00:21:36.110 --> 00:21:39.730
The souls of the authors are disappearing.

00:21:39.730 --> 00:21:41.360
There's no hope left.

00:21:43.480 --> 00:21:44.480
Dazai!

00:21:47.820 --> 00:21:50.820
Dazai! Dazai!

00:21:51.980 --> 00:21:55.000
Gears

00:21:51.980 --> 00:21:55.000
Gears

00:23:25.530 --> 00:23:26.980
Literary Gourmet!

00:23:26.980 --> 00:23:28.860
Happy Birthday, Me!

00:23:29.110 --> 00:23:31.480
Happy birthday, Dazai!

00:23:29.300 --> 00:23:33.970
Strawberry Shortcake: A perfect cake for birthdays,
shareable and topped with lots of strawberries and cream.

00:23:31.480 --> 00:23:34.360
That looks delicious! Let's eat!

00:23:34.860 --> 00:23:35.480
Bwah!?

00:23:35.470 --> 00:23:46.980
"Akutagawa Prize"
"Dazai Osamu"
"June 19th"

00:23:35.530 --> 00:23:36.530
What is this?

00:23:36.530 --> 00:23:39.780
<i>Wakaoi</i> kelp and natto! Your favorites, right?

00:23:39.780 --> 00:23:43.110
Don't mix them together!
And why does the plate say "Akutagawa Prize"?

00:23:43.110 --> 00:23:45.150
You always wanted it, right Dazai- <i>kun</i> ?

00:23:45.150 --> 00:23:47.110
We can't give you the real one,
so we got you this.

00:23:47.110 --> 00:23:49.690
You're messing with me, right?

00:23:49.690 --> 00:23:50.900
That's not true!

00:23:50.900 --> 00:23:53.320
You look a little happy, don't you?

00:23:53.320 --> 00:23:56.360
Sure, I mean I'm happy
you're celebrating my birthday.

00:23:56.360 --> 00:23:59.320
But I want this from someone
I respect, you know?

00:23:59.320 --> 00:24:00.000
Yeah?

00:24:00.000 --> 00:24:00.690
Maybe.
